=== Hunting ===
All '''Pests''' can be [[Charmed]] or [[Lasso]]ed to obtain their [[Attribute Shard]]s and {{Skill XP|+150 Hunting}}. The amount of [[Attribute Shards]] dropped is affected by {{Stat|hunting fortune}}.

== Tips ==
*The maximum damage that can be dealt to '''Pests''' requires an {{Item|InfiniVacuum™ Hooverius}} reforged with {{Item|Clipped Wings}} and {{Item|Bookworm's Favorite Book|amount=5}} applied, {{Level|100}}{{Item|Hedgehog Pet}} equipped, {{Attr|Insect Power X}}, and the {{Item|Book of Progression}} on {{AN|Extra Infliction}}.
**This deals {{Stat|dmg|2,200}}{{confirm}} damage before factoring in the {{Item|Book of Progression}}.

== Trivia ==
*While most non-Pest-specific damage sources do not grant extra damage towards '''Pests''', the {{Item|Book of Progression}}'s {{AN|Extra Infliction}} ability does.
*The base mob type is a {{Item|Bat}} for '''Pests''' that can fly ({{Item|Fly}}, {{Item|Mosquito}}, {{Item|Moth}}) and {{Item|Silverfish}} for the rest.
*If a flying or a running '''Pest''' manages to get out of the plot it spawned in, it will be teleported back into the correct plot within a few seconds. Jumping '''Pests''' return inside the plot on their own unless they cannot, in which case they too get teleported.
*During testing on the [[Alpha Hypixel Network]], {{NPCSprite|Pesthunter Phillip}} allowed an option to prevent a '''Pest''' from spawning during [[Jacob's Farming Contest]]s.

== Bugs ==
* Even though lassoing a mob does not do damage, when hunting '''Pests''' a damage indicator appears. The damage indicator is affected by {{Stat|Crit Damage}} and {{Stat|str}}.

== Notes ==
*The bonus from [[Garden]] bestiary functions differently with different effects:
**Each tier of each of the mobs, including {{MobSprite|Timestalk Clone}} and {{MobSprite|Zombuddy}} grants {{stat|FmF|0.4|icononly=true}}, up to a total of {{Stat|FmF|100}}.
**{{Item|Hedgehog Pet}}'s {{AN|Hunter's Insight}} and {{Item|Brown Bandana}} ignore the above mobs (as they're not '''Pests'''), leading to a total of {{stat|FmF|157.5}} and {{stat|bonus pest chance|45}} respectively.

